This document contains a basic outline for how to install the
EP Analytics characterization tools using the PEBIL binary instrumentation package. 
Direct any questions or comments to allysonc@epanalytics.com

1. System Requirements

   Operating System        Linux
   Binary Format           Elf
   Architecture            ia32 or x86_64

2. PEBIL can be built using autoconf configure script and the resulting makefile.
   A. run the configure script using the flags to define MPICC, MPICXX, CC, & CXX.
   Other useful flags:
       --disable-mpicxxbind if using openmpi gnu

   $ ./configure [MPICC=...] [--enable-mpi=no] [--disable-mpicxxbind]
   Example with Intel Compilers and Intel MPI:
   $./configure MPICC=mpiicc MPICXX=mpiicpc CC=icc CXX=icpc


3. set up environment

   $ source bashrc

4. build

   $ make clean all install

   NOTE: The install target copies things to /path/to/PEBIL/lib/ and 
   /path/to/PEBIL/bin/ (ie, it doesn't do what most install targets
   do in that it doesn't try to system directories and ignores the
   --prefix option to configure).

   If you run into the below error, please reconfigure with 
   --disable-mpicxxbind:

      __pebil__tmp.cxx: In function ‘int main(int, char**)’:
      __pebil__tmp.cxx:7:1: error: ‘MPI’ has not been declared
      MPI::Init(argc, argv); MPI::Finalize();


5. run PEBIL - see the README

